        "no": 1,
        "text": {
          "en": "The Supreme People's Court of the People's Republic of China\nAnnouncement\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Court on the Question Whether an Action for Confirmation of Claim Brought by a Tax Authority in Respect of the Late Payment Surcharge Arising from the Unpaid Tax of a Bankrupt Enterprise Shall Be Accepted was adopted at the 1,548th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 4 June 2012, is hereby promulgated, and shall come into force on 12 July 2012.\n26 June 2012\nThe Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Question Whether an Action for Confirmation of Claim Brought by a Tax Authority\nin Respect of the Late Payment Surcharge Arising from the Unpaid Tax of a Bankrupt\nEnterprise Shall Be Accepted\nFa Shi No. 9 [2012]\n(Adopted at the 1,548th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 4 June 2012; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 26 June 2012; coming into force on 12 July 2012)\nThe Higher People's Court of Qinghai Province:\nThe \"Request for Instructions on the Question Whether an Action for Confirmation of Claim Brought by a Tax Authority in Respect of the Late Payment Surcharge Arising from Tax Shall Be Accepted\" (Qing Min Ta Zi No. 1 [2011]) submitted by your court has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nAn action for confirmation of claim brought by a tax authority in respect of the late payment surcharge arising from the unpaid tax of a bankrupt enterprise shall be accepted by the people's court in accordance with law. In accordance with the relevant provisions of the Enterprise Bankruptcy Law and the Law on the Administration of Tax Collection, the late payment surcharge arising from unpaid tax before the acceptance of a bankruptcy case constitutes an ordinary bankruptcy claim. As for the late payment surcharge arising from unpaid tax after the acceptance of a bankruptcy case, the people's court shall deal with it in accordance with the provisions of Article 61 of the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Trial of Enterprise Bankruptcy Cases.\nThis is our reply."
        },
